<p>One of the best parts of running a rep firm is the days we spend in our dealers' showrooms. This week we sat down with the team at <strong>Colorado Modern Kitchens</strong> to walk through what's new for 2026 — three updates that all touch how their designers quote, sell, and order from us going forward.</p>

<h2>1. The New Pronorm USA Portal</h2>

<p>The first thing on the laptop in the photo above is the new <strong>Pronorm USA portal</strong> — the rebuilt dealer-facing tool every Pronorm dealer in the US will be working in going forward. It's a noticeable upgrade over the previous experience: cleaner project lookups, faster access to current pricing, and a more direct path to the documents and assets dealers actually need on a working day.</p>

<p>If you're a Colorado Modern Kitchens-level Pronorm dealer, you'll be using this every time you quote, order, or pull marketing assets for a Pronorm project. Your territory rep will walk you through credentials and a live login the next time we're in your showroom.</p>

<h2>2. Pronorm: New American Base and Tall Depths</h2>

<img
  src="/images/blog/colorado-modern-kitchens-2026-update/02-display-with-samples.webp"
  alt="Pronorm display in the showroom with white painted upper cabinets, walnut-veneer reeded lower cabinets, and PG3 sample boards staged on the counter"
  loading="lazy"
  width="1600"
  height="1200"
/>

<p>This is the update that designers in our Western US territory have been asking about for years. <a href="/brands/pronorm-german-kitchens">Pronorm</a> is now manufacturing American base and tall cabinet depths — purpose-built for US kitchen architecture and US appliance footprints.</p>

<p>What that means in practice:</p>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Base cabinets</strong> at standard US 24-inch depth (instead of the European 615&nbsp;mm default), so countertops sit flush over standard US dishwashers, ranges, and undercounter refrigeration without filler gymnastics.</li>
  <li><strong>Tall cabinets</strong> at deeper US-spec depths so panel-ready Sub-Zero columns, full-height pantries next to American refrigerators, and oven towers line up cleanly with adjacent runs.</li>
  <li><strong>Same Pronorm everything else</strong> — Winner CAD package, German manufacturing, Pronorm hardware and door styles. The factory in Vlotho is now building these depths into the standard catalog, not a custom one-off.</li>
</ul>

<p>If you've ever lost a job because the Sub-Zero column stuck out an inch past the run, or because the dishwasher created a half-inch gap that your homeowner couldn't unsee, this is the update for you.</p>

<h2>3. PG3 White Oak Veneers</h2>

<p>The third stop on the tour was the new Pronorm <strong>PG3 White Oak Veneer</strong> program — a refresh of how white oak is offered across the line. We brought two of the new finish boards with us:</p>

