<p>A few things worth knowing about PG3:</p>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Vertical-grain rift-cut white oak</strong> as the standard, with the consistent grain reading you'd expect from Pronorm.</li>
  <li><strong>Multiple finish positions in one tier</strong> — light natural through deep stained tones share the same product-group price level, so designers can spec dark or light without pushing a project into a different cost bracket.</li>
  <li><strong>Compatible with the new American depths</strong> — every PG3 finish ships in the new US-spec base and tall sizes from day one. Designers don't have to choose between sizing and finish.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Why This Visit Mattered</h2>

<img
